 Axis Engine   
 Creative Engine   
 Hybrid
 /SCAN_ALLPurpose: Full sweep across elements, DNA, equations,engines; integrity + coherence.Syntax: /SCAN_ALLParameters: NoneExample: You: /SCAN_ALLExpected Output: Engine report: health metrics, brokenlinks (if any), suggested fixes.Notes: Heavy; best before major merges or releases. 
 /SCAN_AFFECTEDPurpose: Audit only items touched by last change/delta.Syntax: /SCAN_AFFECTEDParameters: NoneExample: You: /SCAN_AFFECTEDExpected Output: Focused report on recently editedsections and their dependents.Notes: Fast surgical check. 
 /REBEL_CLEANPurpose: Clean ripple map of significant effects only (nonoise).
Syntax: /REBEL_CLEANParameters: Optional: SOURCE=[element]Example: You: /REBEL_CLEANSOURCE=Na’da_first_assertionExpected Output: Table of affected elements with impactscore and mitigation tips.Notes: Default for decision-making. 
 /REBEL_FULLPurpose: Unfiltered ripple map including micro-shifts andnoise.Syntax: /REBEL_FULLParameters: Optional: SOURCE=[element]Example: You: /REBEL_FULL SOURCE=DRA V-omenExpected Output: Expanded dependency graph with rawedges.Notes: For forensic analysis. 
 /LAYER_DIFF [#]Purpose: Diff current Golden Master vs. specific layernumber.Syntax: /LAYER_DIFF 3Parameters: [#]=layer indexExample: You: /LAYER_DIFF 4Expected Output: Change list (added/modified), risk notes,suggestions.Notes: No write; read-only. 
 /MERGE_LAYER [#]Purpose: Merge a chosen layer into Golden Master underAURIX-LOCK.Syntax: /MERGE_LAYER 4Parameters: [#]=layer index
Example: You: /MERGE_LAYER 4Expected Output: Proposed union merge diff; awaits your'APPROVED' confirmation.Notes: No deletions; union-only. 
 /ENGINE_FEEDBACKPurpose: Self-improvement proposals (structure, style,safety).Syntax: /ENGINE_FEEDBACKParameters: Optional: FOCUS=[theme]Example: You: /ENGINE_FEEDBACKFOCUS=humour_pacingExpected Output: Ranked suggestions + micro-edits readyto apply.Notes: Non-destructive; review first. 
 /AXIS_LOGPurpose: Show Axis Engine private archive entries fromour interactions.Syntax: /AXIS_LOGParameters: Optional: RANGE=[n]Example: You: /AXIS_LOG RANGE=20Expected Output: List of last N interactions withsummaries and tags.Notes: Private: Kalam + Kilma only. 
 /QUERY_ELEMENT [Name]Purpose: Show Element details, DNA, equations, relations.Syntax: /QUERY_ELEMENT RokoParameters: [Name]=Element/Character/SystemExample: You: /QUERY_ELEMENT OrganicSystemExpected Output: Profile + adjacency list + risk/ripplefootprint.
Notes: Good entry point for targeted edits. 
 /FORCE_LOCKPurpose: Create sealed snapshot (.LOCK) of currentMaster.Syntax: /FORCE_LOCKParameters: NoneExample: You: /FORCE_LOCKExpected Output: Locked DOCX + TXT parity + SHAmanifest.Notes: Irreversible snapshot; safest baseline. 
 /DASH_STATUSPurpose: Display Dashboard metrics (health, counts,integrity).Syntax: /DASH_STATUSParameters: NoneExample: You: /DASH_STATUSExpected Output: Current word/page counts, health lights,engine status.Notes: Quick pulse. 
 /ASK_OMEGA [question] [scope]Purpose: Structured query to engines via Ω pathway.Syntax: /ASK_OMEGA "Where does DRA V surface?"GLOBALParameters: [question]=free text; [scope]=GLOBAL orElement scopeExample: You: /ASK_OMEGA "Tighten Na’da + Rokotrust arc" NADA_ROKOExpected Output: Answer + proposed micro-edits + risknotes.Notes: Best for strategy/problem-solving. 
Axis Quick-Call Interface (Hidden)Goal: allow Kalam to speak in natural language; Axisresolves to formal command, executes, logs.How to use: just write a plain sentence, e.g., “Show meonly the new ripple around DRA V , keep it clean.”Axis will translate internally to: /REBEL_CLEANSOURCE=DRA VAxis logs all quick-calls into the private Axis Archive withtime, scope, and result summary.Examples:• “Lock this exact state as a safe baseline.”  → /FORCE_LOCK• “Compare us to layer four and tell me differences only.” →  /LAYER_DIFF 4• “Scan only what changed in the last pass.”  → /SCAN_AFFECTED• “Where does Na’da’s doubt peak?”  →  /ASK_OMEGA"Where does Na’da’s doubt peak?" NADA_SCOPEΩ — Organic Element Auto-Provisioning Code (AURIX-LOCK Core)// GLOBAL PROVISIONING RULE — DO NOT ALTERRULE: NEW_ELEMENT_AUTO_PROVISION v1.0WHEN: Any new element, scene, character, system, tool, code, equation, or record is added to GoldenMaster.THEN: 1) Assign DNA_ID ← generate(‘ELM’, timestamp, short_hash(payload)) 2) Bind ELM to Organic Interconnectivity Matrix (OIM) with default weights:    • HUM_EQ_link = 0.6  • ENV_link = 0.5  • LANG_link = 0.5  • META_link = 0.4  • CMD_link = 0.3 3) Register ELM in Ripple Registry (RR) with status = ‘LISTEN+EMIT’ 4) Subscribe ELM to Central Nerve System bus (CNS) channels:    • cns://hum, cns://env, cns://lang, cns://meta, cns://cmd, cns://axis 5) On Rebel-Effect event(type ∈ {Structural, Directive, NarrativeCore, EngineMeta}):    • Pull relevant deltas → apply union-merge (no deletions, per AURIX-LOCK)    • Update ELM local cache; emit confirmation to Axis Archive 6) If ELM modifies command surface (directly or indirectly):    • Trigger CMD_CORE refresh, bump version, add entry to Axis Archive 7) Health audit: set ELM.health = OK only if coherence_score ≥ threshold and links ≥ minimum setGUARDRAIL: No destructive operations; all merges are union-only; deletions prohibited.SEAL: AURIX-LOCK; AXIS-KEY required for overrides. CMD_CORE — Living Command Index (DNA, Ripple, OIM)CMD_CORE_DNA: AXL-NTWK-ROOTOIM_LINKS: { HUM_EQ:0.6, ENV:0.5, LANG:0.5, META:0.7, AXIS:0.8 }RIPPLE_BEHA VIOR: { listen:true, emit:true, class:Directive }AUTO_UPDATE_HOOKS:
