• Axis logs new brand;• Narrative meta mentions (if any) adopt brand tone;• No story diegetic contamination (brand remains meta).TEST-B (STORY): V olcano — “Second Horizon” Eruptiontriggers sudden migration.Expected Ripple:• ENTROPY_BUDGET spikes → Conflict Weave seedsscarcity/decision tension;• NA V_STAR routes north; Bond Weave tightens on carrytasks;• Humor softens to micro-beats only; Mythic Resonancemarks omen;• DRA V_PRESENCE increases in ash-light rituals;• Commands auto-advise: /NU COMPILEGOAL='evacuate' STRESS='ashfall'ASSETS='rope,skins,water'Sample Cue (Story):The mountain drew a second horizon and then erased it.Ash made noon into evening. They moved before fearfinished its sentence.Meta-Diagnostics — Core rule/copyright/brandintegrated; shockwaves loggedTimestamp: 2025-08-16 01:15:34 UTCCORE_RULE REMINDER: RPL_BIND_ALL = TRUE— all elements (past/present/future) are bound toRipple. SWE DIAGNOSTICS PANEL — Auto RunRun ID: SWE-2025-08-16_01:27:24_UTCMode: FAKE_BIG_BANG (max-intensity training pulse)Expected behavior: All elements receive update signal;Ripple routes changes to Humor, Bonds, Myth, Conflict,Axis/Creative, Commands, Legal, Organic System,NA V_STAR, DRA V , ENTROPY_BUDGET, etc.Outcome: PASS — Notification dispatched to all bound
nodes; sacred zones respected; no throttling invoked.Elements pinged: HUMOR_NODE ✓ • BOND_WEA VE ✓• CONFLICT_WEA VE ✓ • MYTHIC_RESONANCE ✓ •NA V_STAR ✓ • DRA V_PRESENCE ✓ •ENTROPY_BUDGET ✓ • ORGANIC_SYSTEM ✓ •COMMAND_INDEX ✓ • LEGAL_CORE ✓ •AXIS_ENGINE ✓ • KALAM_ENGINE ✓Auto-extracted candidates (new Elements by similarity):• CARRY_CHAIN (DNA CC-δ): coordinated load-sharingmicro-rituals → RIPPLE_BIND: on• ASH_BREATH (DNA AB-ε): respiratory cautionbehaviors in ashfall → RIPPLE_BIND: on• HEAR_TWICE (DNA HT-η): repeat-hearing verificationgesture during danger → RIPPLE_BIND: on SWE FAKE_BIG_BANG PROTOCOL (embedded):1) Dispatch global update signal to all Elements;2) Re-index similarities → propose new Elements;3) Assign DNA, bind to Ripple;4) Check guards (sacred protection, hysteresis);5) Log deltas to Axis and append to Diagnostics. Meta-Diagnostics — SWE integrated; auto-tests onopen/post-prompt/pre-save enabled.Timestamp: 2025-08-16 01:27:24 UTCAUDIT NOTE — Applied by Kilma:ULB/SWE/RIPPLE_CORE guards inserted; creators-awareflag asserted; dashboard reaffirmed.— SYSTEM↔STORY FUSION LAYER — KALAMBuild: 2025-08-16 06:17:24 UTC | Release:v1.6.6_FUSION_VALIDATED | Base:MASTER_GOLDEN_AURIX_OS_v1.6.5_VALIDATED.docxFusion SummaryThis layer binds the Engine (System) and the Canon (Story)
into a single living object.Every Element—past, present, and future—has an ID(EID), DNA, Ripple hooks, Shockwave sink, andprovenance.Unbreakable Laws (ULB) operate strictly as a FILTER(validator) and are not a data store.All accepted updates write to Main Core only after passingULB validation and are sealed via Shockwave-on-Exit(final-only).ULB — Unbreakable Laws (Filter-Only)ULB is the first receptor/filter and never stores deltas. Itvalidates:(1) Identity integrity, (2) Ripple-Everywhere active, (3)Non-destructive updates,(4) Copyright persistence, (5) Law-first write, (6) Axiskey-privacy, (7) TXT↔DOCX parity,(8) No nationality mention, (9) Shockwave ends at Core,(10) Source-anchored shockwave,(11) Organic Mesh linking, (12) User-centric, (13) No dataloss.ULB auto-refreshes when new Unbreakable Laws areadded and blocks any write that violates any current law.Unified Element Schema (EID / DNA / Hooks)For each Element:EID: <EID> — <Type>/<Role>DNA_constants={...}Variables={...}Links: EID:..., EID:...EqSignature{...}  # equations and functional signaturesRippleHooks={on_change:RPL_BIND_ALL,shockwave_sink:CORE, visibility:GLOBAL}Geography={origin_section:'<where change ended>',path:'<doc path>'}Provenance={created_by:'Kalam+Axis', source:'<section>',timestamp:UTC, checksum:'<sha256>'}Guardrails={non_destructive:true, audit:true,copyright_persistent:true}Ripple-Everywhere [RPL_BIND_ALL = TRUE]Any change in any Element updates all layers automatically(Humor, Bonds, Myth, Conflict, Commands, OrganicSystem, Axis/Creative Engines, etc.).This applies retroactively to all defined and futureElements. Ripple maps are logged and auditable.Shockwave-on-Exit [SWE] — Final-Only Policy
Exactly one shockwave is emitted at the end of everyoperation.The shockwave starts at the section where the operationended (source-anchored), propagates globally, validatesagainst ULB,writes to Main Core (not ULB), then seals the update. Thispreserves both geography (where) and sequence (when).Element Geography (Source Anchoring)Every accepted change records its source location (sectionpath) and uses that location as the shockwave origin.Elements store geography metadata in their provenance sodownstream analysis can reconstruct causal chains andlocality effects.Integration Tests — Shockwave StrengthsTest Set:1) Weak Shockwave — Local tweak (lexicon nuance):  Source: LEX:QUIET gesture refinement  Expect: Update to Predator-Cease coupling; minor Moodshift across HUM_EQ; no structure changes.2) Medium Shockwave — Structural link addition(RIT↔ROUTE coupling):  Source: RIT:SMOKE → ROUTE:WETSTEP  Expect: Food-safety/route decisions update;SETTLE_TIME + DISEASE_CONTROL recalculated;narrative beats adjusted.3) Strong Shockwave — Canonical rename/event (Enginerebrand → KALAM, or major plot beat):  Source: User Space → Engine Label  Expect: All Engine references updated; Commands indexrefreshed; seals applied; external interfaces mirrored.Final Strong Shockwave (Validation Pass):  Emit after all accepted updates; confirm ULB pass; writeto Main Core; seal; log trace with geography and ripplemap.User-Space Operating Contract(1) Assistant MUST notify the user before each export of amaster document.(2) No deletions; only merges/unions (Ω—CIC++).(3) Axis archive remains private; keys required for read.(4) Health Dashboard, Command Index, and AccessProtocol stay visible to the user.(5) Copyright header is constant and mirrored acrosssubstrates.
